# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
# Test artefacts: claim-log probes written by the domain-regression tests
_*probe_*.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
build/
dist/

# Python packaging: the cdylib staged into the wheel by python/build_wheel.py, and its
# provenance record. DESIGN.md §7.8 forbids a checked-in binary because silent drift from
# its source changes what runs; a wheel is a binary from the consumer's point of view, so
# it is a BUILD PRODUCT here and never a tree artifact. `git status` after a wheel build is
# the check on that. The provenance record is what makes the drift detectable once the
# binary has left the tree.
python/src/onnxruntime_ep_vulkan/_lib/
python/dist/

# Squad: ignore runtime state (logs, inbox, sessions)
# Note: .squad/casting/* is identity and MUST be committed to main, not ignored
.squad/orchestration-log/
.squad/log/
.squad/decisions/inbox/
.squad/sessions/
.squad/.scratch/
.squad/.cache/
# Squad: SubSquad activation file (local to this machine)
.squad-workstream

# Bench: transient Vulkan device-probe scratch dirs
bench/vkfacts-*/

# Bench: probe taps and per-arm counters. These are large .npy dumps of intermediate
# activations rewritten by every probe run; the findings that depend on them live in the
# committed bench/results/*.json records, which carry the numbers rather than the arrays.
bench/scratch/

# Test: local pytest capture files
tests/_run_*.txt

# ORT profiling artifacts (written to CWD by enable_profiling)
onnxruntime_profile__*.json
vulkan_test*.json
island_attribution.json
trace_*.json

# CI lane evidence (criterion 10 gate artifacts, Link 2026-07-31).
# Written by ci/gate_chain_fp32.py into bench/results/ci-lane/ on a runner and
# uploaded as a build artifact. Never committed: probe output goes to
# bench/results/ or a temp path, never the repo root.
bench/results/ci-lane/
bench/results/link-gate/
gate_chain_fp32_profile_*.json
bench/results/claim_log_attribution.jsonl

# Mouse: models fetched for op-census work. Large, and reproducible from the URL recorded in
# bench/results/model_provenance.json — an artifact belongs in the repo, a 14 MB blob does not.
.scratch-models/

# Raw tensor dumps from probes: regenerable, and one kv.npz reached 2.8 GB.
# They are inputs to a verdict, not the verdict; the JSON records are the evidence.
bench/results/**/*.npy
bench/results/**/*.npz

